title: "AURKB–PDAC computational workflow"

type: software

author:
Fajad Fardin
ORCID : 0009-0008-3060-1989
email : fahad47ju@gmail.com

abstract: >-
  Computational notebooks and reproducibility documentation for a chemotype-aware
  QSAR–GCN consensus screening workflow for prioritizing natural-product-derived
  AURKB-targeting candidates for pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma. The repository
  covers COCONUT natural-product prescreening, descriptor-based classical QSAR
  analysis with scaffold-disjoint validation, and graph convolutional network
  evaluation with QSAR–GCN consensus prioritization. The workflow reduced 738,827
  COCONUT records to 86,056 prescreened compounds, retained a hash-verified
  6,232-compound QSAR-to-GCN transfer set, and identified 615 Tier 1 and
  29 Tier 1A candidates. Executed notebook outputs and provenance information are
  retained to support verification of the reported workflow.

keywords:
  - "Aurora kinase B"
  - "AURKB"
  - "pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma"
  - "QSAR"
  - "graph convolutional network"
  - "consensus screening"
  - "natural products"

license: BSD-3-Clause

